ists.infradead.org</div>=0A<div>&nbsp;</div>=0A<div>VOP2 fetches the scano=
ut data for all of its video ports over a single</div>=0A<div>AXI clock.&n=
bsp; On RK3588 that clock is pinned to 500 MHz by the device tree</div>=0A=
<div>and nothing ever raises it, so a mode whose pixel rate outruns what t=
he</div>=0A<div>AXI clock can deliver underruns the internal scanout FIFO.=
&nbsp; The hardware</div>=0A<div>reports this as POST_BUF_EMPTY and the pi=
cture is corrupted.</div>=0A<div>&nbsp;</div>=0A<div>3840x2160@120 over Di=
splayPort is such a mode.&nbsp; Measured on an Orange Pi</div>=0A<div>5 Pl=
us by moving the rate at runtime while the mode was up, with dclk</div>=0A=
<div>unchanged at 594 MHz throughout, so that the AXI rate was the only</d=
iv>=0A<div>variable:</div>=0A<div>&nbsp;</div>=0A<div>&nbsp; 500 MHz: ~594=
000 suppressed vop2_isr callbacks per 5 s, corrupted</div>=0A<div>&nbsp; 7=
50 MHz: no POST_BUF_EMPTY at all for the 42 s the phase lasted, clean</div=
>=0A<div>&nbsp; 500 MHz: ~607000 suppressed callbacks per 5 s, corrupted a=
gain</div>=0A<div>&nbsp;</div>=0A<div>Both transitions are immediate.&nbsp=
; Heiko Stuebner reports the same</div>=0A<div>starvation on different har=
dware [1].</div>=0A<div>&nbsp;</div>=0A<div>The requirement follows each p=
ort's pixel rate rather than its interface</div>=0A<div>clock, and it is p=
er port rather than aggregate.&nbsp; Two measurements at</div>=0A<div>500 =
MHz pin that down:</div>=0A<div>&nbsp;</div>=0A<div>&nbsp; - a single port=
 scanning out 3840x2160@120 underruns, while the same</div>=0A<div>&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp; composed pixel rate spread over three ports - 3840x2160@60 on =
one</div>=0A<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; and 3840x2160@30 on two others - is cl=
ean for a minute with no</div>=0A<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; underrun on any o=
f them.&nbsp; The totals are equal to the pixel:</div>=0A<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;=
